@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Docker Security";
    ViewData["ActiveMenu"] = "AzureDevOps";
}

<div class="container py-4">
    <p class="text-center lead">
        Securing your Docker environment is critical for protecting applications, infrastructure, and data.
        This includes image scanning, access control, secure communication, and container isolation.
    </p>
    <hr />

    <!-- Section: Container Security Best Practices -->
    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2>Container Security Best Practices</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>Use trusted base images from official repositories</li>
            <li>Minimize images — only include necessary binaries and files</li>
            <li>Run containers as non-root users</li>
            <li>Keep images and dependencies up to date</li>
            <li>Apply the principle of least privilege in all configurations</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <!-- Section: Managing User Permissions -->
    <div class="mt-5">
        <h3>Managing User Permissions</h3>
        <p>By default, containers run as root, which can be a security risk. To run as a non-root user:</p>
        <div class="code-snippet bg-light p-3 rounded position-relative">
            <pre class="mb-0"><code>FROM node:18
RUN useradd -m appuser
USER appuser
CMD ["node", "app.js"]</code></pre>
            <button class="btn btn-outline-secondary copy-btn position-absolute top-0 end-0 m-2">Copy</button>
        </div>
        <p>Also, avoid adding users to the <code>docker</code> group unnecessarily on the host system.</p>
    </div>

    <!-- Section: Scanning Images for Vulnerabilities -->
    <div class="mt-5">
        <h3>Scanning Images for Vulnerabilities</h3>
        <p>Use tools to scan your Docker images before deployment:</p>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Docker Scout:</strong> Integrated into Docker Desktop and CLI</li>
            <li><strong>Trivy (by Aqua):</strong> Lightweight, fast scanner</li>
            <li><strong>Snyk:</strong> CLI and GitHub integration for CI scanning</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Example: Scan with Trivy</p>
        <div class="code-snippet bg-light p-3 rounded position-relative">
            <pre class="mb-0"><code>trivy image myapp:latest</code></pre>
            <button class="btn btn-outline-secondary copy-btn position-absolute top-0 end-0 m-2">Copy</button>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Section: Securing Network Communication -->
    <div class="mt-5">
        <h3>Securing Network Communication</h3>
        <ul>
            <li>Use internal Docker networks for container communication</li>
            <li>Limit open ports and expose only what's needed</li>
            <li>Use TLS for communication with private registries</li>
            <li>Encrypt sensitive environment variables or use Docker secrets</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <!-- Section: Role-Based Access Control (RBAC) -->
    <div class="mt-5">
        <h3>Implementing Role-Based Access Control (RBAC)</h3>
        <p>When using Docker with tools like Portainer, Kubernetes, or hosted registries, enable RBAC to limit actions:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>Define roles (admin, dev, ops) with scoped access</li>
            <li>Limit registry access to specific teams or namespaces</li>
            <li>Audit container usage and changes</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <!-- Summary -->
    <div class="mt-5">
        <p>
            A secure Docker workflow includes hardened images, proper access control, ongoing vulnerability scanning,
            and least-privilege practices. Proactive security is essential for DevOps and production deployments.
        </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Navigation Buttons -->
    <div class="d-flex justify-content-between mt-4">
        <a href="@Url.Action("DockerRegistryHub", "AzureDevOps")" class="btn btn-outline-secondary">
            &larr; Previous: Docker Registry & Hub
        </a>
        <a href="@Url.Action("DockerSwarm", "AzureDevOps")" class="btn btn-outline-secondary">
            Next: Docker Swarm (Orchestration) &rarr;
        </a>
    </div>
</div>

<!-- Copy Script -->
<script>
    document.querySelectorAll('.copy-btn').forEach(btn => {
        btn.addEventListener('click', function () {
            const codeText = this.parentElement.querySelector('code')?.innerText;
            if (codeText) {
                navigator.clipboard.writeText(codeText).then(() => {
                    alert('Code copied to clipboard!');
                });
            }
        });
    });
</script>
